      "gap": "Annex lines 175-182 assert, without derivation, that every future indicator B_{n+j} (j>=1) has conditional mean a/T and variance ab/T^2 given F_n and that every distinct future pair has conditional joint success probability a(a+1)/(T(T+1)). The written argument (annex 167-173) gives only the conditional probability of a specified future word of length m (and the K_{n,m} count law); no step derives the conditional marginal of B_{n+j} for j>=2 or of a non-adjacent future pair (no conditional exchangeability of the future given F_n, no marginalization over intermediate draws, no written integration of the conditional Bernoulli product against the updated beta(a,b) density). The full proof promised by proved=annex:p15.polya-posterior-prediction of E(K_{n,m}|F_n)=ma/T, Var(K_{n,m}|F_n)=mab(T+m)/(T^2(T+1)) and the m>1 excess over mX_n(1-X_n) must be completely written.",
